# CyberFlap

Virtual split-flap display web app. Own product — never refer to competing brands in code, comments, UI, or filenames.

## Stack

- Vite + React (JavaScript, not TypeScript)
- React Router: `/` (board), `/settings`
- `BrowserRouter` `basename` comes from `import.meta.env.BASE_URL` (unset locally; `/cyberflap` in production)
- No backend; persistence via `localStorage`
- Public repo: `https://github.com/michael714/cyberflap` (`origin` is SSH)

## GitHub Pages

Live site: `https://michael714.github.io/cyberflap/`

- Pages **must** deploy the Vite `dist/` build via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`), with Pages source set to **GitHub Actions** (`build_type: workflow`)
- Do **not** serve the `main` branch root as Pages — that ships uncompiled JSX (`/src/main.jsx`) and a blank white page, and a leftover “pages build and deployment” job can overwrite a good Actions deploy
- `vite.config.js`: `base` is `/` for `npm run dev`, `/cyberflap/` for `vite build`; after build, copy `dist/index.html` → `dist/404.html` so `/settings` deep links work
- `package.json` `homepage` matches the Pages URL

## Layout (`src/`)

- `components/` — `Board`, `Tile` (+ CSS)
- `content/` — clock, weather, message, rainbow, agenda, display mode, rotation hooks, `config.js`
- `pages/` — `BoardPage`, `SettingsPage`
- `utils/` — `characters.js`, `board.js`, `useBoard.js`, `flipSound.js`

## Board model

- Fixed **22 columns**; dynamic **1–6 rows** (no empty trailing rows)
- Wrap/truncate via `layoutText()` in `utils/board.js` (`MAX_ROWS = 6`)
- Tile codes in `utils/characters.js`: blank `0`, A–Z `1–26`, digits `27–36` (1–9 then 0), punctuation, colors `63–70`
- Helpers: `tileFromChar`, `tileFromColor`, `getFlipPath`, `FLIP_SEQUENCE`
- Tile size: ~3:2, CSS `clamp` on `--tile-w` (viewport-based, not row-count-based)
- Wider **row-gap** than column-gap; board height CSS-transitions (~260ms) on row count change

## Flip animation

- Each step uses CSS `rotateX` split-flap (top then bottom half), ~72ms (`FLIP_STEP_MS`)
- Walk shortest path on `FLIP_SEQUENCE`; stagger starts per cell
- Only tiles whose codes change should animate (`useBoard` skips equal boards)
- Per flip **step** (not whole tile): `playFlipClick()` from `utils/flipSound.js`

## Content rotation

Order: `clock` → `weather` → `message` (`MODULE_ORDER`). Defaults in `content/config.js` (10s dwell, etc.).

| Module | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| clock | 1-line time with seconds; tick 1s while active |
| weather | Open-Meteo + geolocation (SF fallback); refresh 15m |
| message | Demo: custom string from `localStorage`. Agenda: current published page |

Display mode (`cyberflap.displayMode`, default `demo`):

- **Demo** — clock, weather, custom message, Manual override; Next/Prev walk modules
- **Agenda** — pages from repo-root `agenda.txt`; Next/Prev walk the deck (not auto-advanced); clock/weather still rotate with the **current page only**; Agenda-only holds that page

Manual override (demo only) shows a sample ~10s then resumes. Playback Pause persists in agenda mode (`cyberflap.agendaPaused`). Next/Prev reset the auto-advance timer.

## Classroom agenda (`agenda.txt`)

- File lives at the **repo root** (not `public/`). Replace it on github.com (pencil or **Add file → Upload files**); no git CLI required
- Production fetches `raw.githubusercontent.com/.../agenda.txt` (GitHub API raw fallback); does **not** wait for a Vite/Pages rebuild. Poll every `AGENDA_POLL_MS` (2m). Keep last good deck if a poll fails
- Dev: Vite serves `/agenda.txt` from the repo root (`npm run dev` on **5173** only — extra ports leave hidden Cursor Browser tabs still playing flip sound)
- Format: `=== LABEL` starts a page; body until the next header; lines before the first `===` are ignored; no headers → one page
- **No page-count cap.** Each page is still **6 rows × 22 columns**; extra lines truncate (they do not spill to the next page). The `===` label is status chrome only, not a board row
- Empty/missing file → on-board notice, not a blank page
- Panel prefs: `cyberflap.agendaPageIndex`, `cyberflap.agendaOnly`, `cyberflap.agendaPaused`
- Keyboard/clicker in agenda mode: Left/Right or PageUp/PageDown

## Rainbow mode (`cyberflap.rainbowMode`, default on)

- Off or **1 row** → neutral tiles
- **6 rows** → full spectrum, per-color ink OK
- **2–5 rows** → colors from one contrast group so **all rows share one text color**
  - Dark/white ink: red, violet
  - Light/black ink: orange, yellow, green, blue
  - 5 rows: light group + best extra for black ink (red), single black ink

## Settings (`/settings`)

- Display mode radios (Demo / Classroom agenda) persist immediately
- Demo: custom message + Save → `cyberflap.customMessage`; live wrap preview
- Agenda: read-only preview of published `agenda.txt` pages
- Rainbow checkbox (persists immediately)

## Sound

- Web Audio only (no audio files): ~30ms filtered-noise clack
- Cap concurrent voices / scale gain; unlock `AudioContext` on first user gesture
- Mute: `cyberflap.mute` (default unmuted); toggle next to playback

## Brand / UI

- Wordmark + cyan/magenta/dark-navy look (Orbitron + Share Tech Mono)
- Gear → settings; don’t let chrome overpower the board

## Prompt history (canonical)

1 scaffold → 2 grid/chars → 3 rebrand+flip → 4 content+rotation → 5 dynamic rows → 6 settings route → 7 row gap+rainbow → 8 ink groups+playback → 9 flip sound → 10 classroom agenda deck

When extending: keep board codes/layout central, prefer `localStorage` for prefs, match existing visual language, number future prompts.
